# /enroll and /consult are public marketing pages but thin lead forms
# (the application form and a booking form) that duplicate /assessment,
# the indexed lead page. noindex keeps them out of results; follow keeps
# the links on them counting. Neither is in the sitemap.
/enroll
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, follow
/consult
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, follow

# Security headers — apply to all routes
# Permissions-Policy: camera=(self) etc. allows THIS SITE to request
# camera/microphone/screen-share (the Smartious Classroom needs all
# three) while still denying them to any third-party content.
# NOTE: camera=() [empty] blocks EVERYONE INCLUDING OUR OWN SITE and
# silently kills getUserMedia with no prompt — that value was the
# root cause of the classroom never getting camera access.
# X-Frame-Options SAMEORIGIN (not DENY): other sites still cannot
# frame Smartious pages (clickjacking protection intact), but OUR OWN
# same-origin iframes keep working — the library's pdf.js book viewer
# loads /pdfjs/index.html in an iframe. DENY here blocked it, because
# Netlify merges every matching _headers rule and sends ALL values;
# a per-path SAMEORIGIN "override" below cannot cancel a global DENY,
# the browser just receives both and refuses to frame.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(self), display-capture=(self), fullscreen=(self), geolocation=()

